Comments:
    This is a 2D test problem for the handling of advection in non-equidistant
    grids. The setup here differs from the original test problem in that we
    consider only half of the original domain; the original problem requires
    the left half of the y_min boundary to be a prescribed-theta inlet and the
    right half to be a zero-gradient outlet, which is difficult to implement in
    Pencil. Also note that the actual benchmark problem is a steady-state problem.
    
    Comparing contour plots of var.cc in the final snapshot in simulations with
    and without upwinding, one clearly sees that upwinding reduces the extent of
    regions where the passive scalar takes a negative value (this can even be
    seen from the ccmin diagnostic)
References:
    R. M. Smith & A. G. Hutton (1982) The Numerical Treatment Of Advection: A
    Performance Comparison Of Current Methods, Numerical Heat Transfer, 5:4, 439-461
